// Renode platform description for ATSAM4E8E (Cortex-M4).
//
// Renode upstream has no SAM4E platform; sam4s.repl is the closest
// neighbor (same M4 core, identical UART/PMC/EFC base addresses on
// the system controller side - 0x400E0xxx) but is unsuitable as an
// `using` base because of address conflicts with SAM4E peripherals:
//
//   - SAM4E PIOD lives at 0x400E1400 where SAM4S has RSTC. The
//     SAM4S_RSTC model would consume PIOD writes klipper makes for
//     pin muxing, with unpredictable side effects.
//   - SAM4E WDT lives at 0x400E1850 where SAM4S has nothing
//     mapped; SAM4S WDT at 0x400E1450 conversely has no SAM4E
//     analog. The SAM4S_WDT model would tick on its default
//     timeout because klipper SAM4E firmware writes to a different
//     address (0x400E1850) and never feeds the SAM4S WDT - that
//     could trigger spurious resets via the rstc connection.
//   - SAM4E ADC peripheral is AFEC0/AFEC1 at 0x400B0000/0x400B4000,
//     not the SAM4S_ADC at 0x40038000. Renode does not ship a
//     SAM_AFEC model, so AFEC stubs are runtime-injected by the
//     launcher (_AFEC_BASES_FOR_CHIP, mirroring the SAME70 path).
//
// Standalone with only what klipper SAM4E firmware actually drives:
// CPU + NVIC + DWT + memory (boot mirror at 0x0 + flash at
// 0x400000 + sram at 0x20000000) + UART0 (host link, PA9/PA10) +
// PMC_SR flipflop (so SystemInit's MOSCXTS/MOSCSELS/MCKRDY/LOCKA
// busy-wait loops complete) + SAM4S_EEFC (so bootloader_request's
// FRDY wait completes; reusing the SAM4S model since the EEFC
// register layout is identical between SAM4S and SAM4E).
//
// Klipper SAM4E uses generic/armcm_timer.c (DWT + SysTick), so
// no chip-specific timer modeling is required. Watchdog (WDT)
// writes go to unmapped 0x400E1850 and produce harmless log
// warnings; the firmware never reads WDT back.

cpu: CPU.CortexM @ sysbus
    cpuType: "cortex-m4"
    nvic: nvic

nvic: IRQControllers.NVIC @ sysbus 0xE000E000
    -> cpu@0
    systickFrequency: 120000000

dwt: Miscellaneous.DWT @ sysbus 0xE0001000
    frequency: 120000000

// SAM4E8E: 512KB flash linked at 0x00400000 (klipper's
// CONFIG_FLASH_APPLICATION_ADDRESS for MACH_SAM4). The boot
// region at 0x0 mirrors flash on real hardware via GPNVM bit 1;
// here we stand it up as separate Memory.MappedMemory so any
// stray access at 0x0 doesn't fault. Renode's LoadELF sets the
// CPU PC directly to the ELF entry point at 0x400000 so the
// boot mirror itself never executes.
boot: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x0
    size: 0x400000

flash: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x400000
    size: 0x100000

sram: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x20000000
    size: 0x20000

// PMC_SR is a status-bit register that klipper's SystemInit busy-
// waits on. flipflop.py alternates 0/0xFFFFFFFF between reads, so
// every "is bit X set" check eventually sees a non-zero readback
// and the wait loops complete. Same approach upstream sam4s.repl
// uses for SAM4S; works here unchanged because the SAM4E PMC has
// PMC_SR at the same offset (0x400E0468).
PMC_SR: Python.PythonPeripheral @ sysbus 0x400E0468
    size: 0x4
    initable: true
    filename: "scripts/pydev/flipflop.py"

uart0: UART.SAM_USART @ sysbus 0x400E0600
    uartOnlyMode: true
    enablePdc: true
    ->nvic@8

eefc: Miscellaneous.SAM4S_EEFC @ sysbus 0x400E0A00
    underlyingMemory: flash
    ->nvic@6
